CORE-MATH (MIT)
---------------

Project:  CORE-MATH, correctly rounded mathematical functions,
          https://core-math.gitlabpages.inria.fr/ (git:
          https://gitlab.inria.fr/core-math/core-math)
Ported:   at commit 1f876c544231f310f483f0a523e163850141dd7e (2026-10-26), to Rust,
          rounding to nearest only, without errno or exception flags (M4-P1, H36):
          - crates/ep9_math/src/exp.rs from src/binary64/exp/exp.c (cr_exp);
          - crates/ep9_math/src/log.rs from src/binary64/log/log.c and
            src/binary64/log/dint.h (cr_log);
          - crates/ep9_math/src/pow.rs from src/binary64/pow/pow.c, pow.h, dint.h
            and qint.h (cr_pow).
          and, at the same commit (M4-P4, H36), from src/binary64/<name>/<name>.c
          (cr_<name>) unless stated:
          - crates/ep9_math/src/{acos,acosh,asin,asinh,atan,atanh,cbrt,cosh,expm1,
            log10,log1p,log2,sin,sinh,tan,tanh}.rs;
          - crates/ep9_math/src/atan2.rs from src/binary64/atan2/atan2.c and
            src/binary64/atan2/tint.h (cr_atan2);
          - crates/ep9_math/src/cos.rs from src/binary64/cos/cos.c (cr_cos), and
            crates/ep9_math/src/trig.rs from the parts of cos.c that tan.c repeats
